<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S4.F2.fig2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 2</span>: </span><span id="S4.F2.fig2.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Training acceleration comparison. Our method reaches both FID <math id="S4.F2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq 10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq 10</annotation></semantics></math> and FID <math id="S4.F2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq 3</annotation></semantics></math> substantially earlier than DMD2, indicating faster convergence for one step generation.</span></figcaption>
