<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Anchor-margin weight.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A2.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ Anchor-margin weight. ‣ Appendix B Additional ImageNet Ablations ‣ Teacher-Feature Drifting: One-Step Diffusion Distillation with Pretrained Diffusion Representations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> studies the effect of the anchor-margin weight. The FID differences are modest, but nonzero anchor-margin weights improve the later-stage budgeted FID, with <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\mathrm{anchor}}=1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>anchor</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\mathrm{anchor}}=1.0</annotation></semantics></math> giving the best result before <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="200" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>200</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">200</annotation></semantics></math>K updates. Together with the diversity visualization in Figure <a href="#S4.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ 4.3 Ablation Study ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Teacher-Feature Drifting: One-Step Diffusion Distillation with Pretrained Diffusion Representations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, this suggests that the anchor-margin term mainly improves coverage and reduces missing-mode behavior while maintaining competitive image quality.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.T5" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A2.T5.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 5</span>: </span><span id="A2.T5.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Anchor-margin weight ablation on class-conditional ImageNet-<math id="A2.T5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="64\times 64" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>64</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>64</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">64\times 64</annotation></semantics></math>. All rows use one step sampling, drift feature levels Enc-11 + Bottleneck + Dec-7, drift radii <math id="A2.T5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{0.02,0.05,0.2\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="1.110em" minsize="1.110em">{</mo><mn>0.02</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.05</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.2</mn><mo maxsize="1.110em" minsize="1.110em">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{0.02,0.05,0.2\}</annotation></semantics></math>, and feature-noise at 0.5. Each entry reports the best FID observed no later than the specified update budget.</span></figcaption>
<table id="A2.T5.5" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
