<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Generator learning rate.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A2.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ Generator learning rate. ‣ Appendix B Additional ImageNet Ablations ‣ Teacher-Feature Drifting: One-Step Diffusion Distillation with Pretrained Diffusion Representations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> reports a diagnostic learning-rate comparison. The default learning rate <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\times 10^{-6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\times 10^{-6}</annotation></semantics></math> gives the strongest overall result among the available runs, while <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5\times 10^{-6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\times 10^{-6}</annotation></semantics></math> is less stable and yields worse final FID. Since these runs are not a fully controlled sweep over all other hyperparameters, we use this comparison only as an appendix diagnostic and keep the main text focused on the fully matched ablations above.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.T6" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A2.T6.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 6</span>: </span><span id="A2.T6.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Diagnostic generator learning-rate comparison on class-conditional ImageNet-<math id="A2.T6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="64\times 64" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>64</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>64</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">64\times 64</annotation></semantics></math>. All rows use one step sampling and the five-level feature configuration Enc-6 + Enc-11 + Bottleneck + Dec-7 + Dec-12. Each entry reports the best FID observed no later than the specified update budget.</span></figcaption>
<table id="A2.T6.5" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
